jobs.description:
The Vice President of Sales and Marketing is responsible for defining and leading the company’s overall sales and marketing strategy. This role oversees sales growth, market expansion, brand promotion, customer acquisition, and the development of commercial channels, with the objective of continuously enhancing sales performance and market competitiveness.

The position requires the integration of sales and marketing functions, aligning market strategies with business goals. By optimizing sales systems, strengthening brand influence, expanding the customer base, and driving marketing initiatives, the incumbent will foster revenue growth, increase market share, and ensure long-term business development.

Core Responsibilities

I. Sales and Marketing Strategy
- Formulate annual and long-term sales and marketing development strategies for the company.
- Translate corporate business objectives into actionable plans for sales growth and market expansion.
- Define target markets, customer segments, and key directions for business growth.
- Establish mechanisms to ensure synergy between sales and marketing functions.
- Monitor the execution of strategies and adjust direction in response to changing market conditions.

II. Sales Management and Performance Growth
- Lead the company’s sales organization, setting sales targets and performance plans.
- Optimize sales processes, customer development, and the management of business opportunities.
- Drive the acquisition and management of key accounts, strategic clients, and major commercial partnerships.
- Oversee the performance of the sales team, focusing on improving sales conversion rates and customer retention.
- Develop systems for sales forecasting, performance analysis, and evaluation.

III. Marketing and Brand Promotion
- Develop strategies for corporate marketing and brand promotion.
- Lead market research, competitive analysis, and market positioning efforts.
- Drive digital marketing, content marketing, and integrated marketing campaigns.
- Enhance brand awareness, market influence, and customer perception.
- Ensure that all marketing activities remain consistent with the company’s brand positioning.

IV. Market Expansion and Business Development
- Identify new markets, customer segments, and potential business opportunities.
- Drive regional market expansion and the development of new business channels.
- Establish strategic partnerships and industry collaborations.
- Evaluate market demand, industry trends, and the activities of competitors.
- Facilitate the commercialization of the company’s products and services within target markets.

V. Customer Relations and Commercial Channels
- Establish enterprise-level customer relationship management and customer acquisition strategies;
- Drive the maintenance of key accounts and the development of long-term partnerships;
- Optimize sales channels, distribution systems, and partner networks;
- Enhance customer satisfaction, repeat purchase rates, and customer lifetime value;
- Collaborate with customer success and business operations teams to improve the customer experience.

VI. Sales and Marketing Performance Management
- Develop KPIs and performance management systems for the sales and marketing departments;
- Monitor revenue growth, sales conversion rates, customer acquisition costs (CAC), and marketing ROI;
- Analyze sales data and the effectiveness of marketing campaigns;
- Identify performance gaps and formulate improvement initiatives;
- Report on sales and marketing performance regularly to the CEO, COO, and the Board of Directors.

VII. Budget and Resource Management
- Formulate annual budgets and resource allocation plans for sales and marketing;
- Oversee marketing expenditures, costs of sales, and departmental operating expenses;
- Optimize marketing budgets and the return on marketing investment;
- Efficiently allocate sales personnel, marketing resources, and technical tools;
- Ensure that sales and marketing investments support the company’s overall growth objectives.

VIII. Team Building and Cross-functional Collaboration
- Lead the management teams for sales, marketing, and business development;
- Manage Senior Directors, Directors, Regional Sales Leaders, and Marketing Managers;
- Establish programs for sales talent development, performance incentives, and leadership pipeline building;
- Maintain close collaboration with the product, finance, operations, and customer success departments;
- Align sales and marketing teams toward unified commercial growth goals.

Qualifications

Education
- Bachelor’s degree or higher in Marketing, Business Administration, Management, Economics, or a related field;
- MBA, Master’s degree in Marketing, or a related management degree is preferred;
- Professional training in sales management, strategic marketing, or business management is a plus.

Work Experience
- 20+ years of experience in sales, marketing, or business management;
- 15+ years of experience in senior sales and marketing management;
- Prior experience in roles such as VP of Sales and Marketing, VP of Sales, VP of Marketing, or Chief Commercial Officer is preferred;
- Proven experience in leading large-scale sales and marketing teams, as well as managing cross-regional operations;
- Demonstrated success in developing business growth strategies, expanding market reach, and driving corporate revenue growth.

Core Competencies
- Sales Strategy & Revenue Growth;
- Marketing Strategy & Brand Management;
- Business Development;
- Market Expansion;
- Customer Acquisition & Retention;
- Sales Performance Management;
- Digital Marketing;
- Strategic Partnerships;
- Budget & ROI Management;
- Market Research & Competitive Analysis;
- Cross-functional Leadership;
- Executive Team Management.

Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
- Annual sales revenue growth rate;
- Market share growth rate;
- Number of new customer acquisitions;
- Sales conversion rate;
- Customer Acquisition Cost (CAC);
- Customer retention rate;
- Marketing ROI;
- Brand awareness and market influence;
- Sales target achievement rate;
- Success rate of new market expansion;
- Growth rate of strategic partnership channels;
- Overall performance achievement rate of sales and marketing teams.

